# One virtual pickup, triggered manually.
#
# NO BACKSLASHES ANYWHERE IN THIS FILE, not even in a comment. rosidl_adapter
# copies these comments into the generated IDL and the result is decoded with
# Python's 'unicodeescape' codec, so a shell line-continuation at the end of a
# comment line is an invalid escape and the whole package fails to build --
# minutes into a container build, on the robot. test_interfaces.py checks this.
#
# Two ways to start one. The topic is the operational path (Nav2 finishes, then
# a script triggers this); the action is the better one by hand, because it
# streams feedback and Ctrl-C cancels:
#   ros2 topic pub --once /pallet_approach/start std_msgs/String "{data: pickup}"
#   ros2 action send_goal /pallet_task pallet_approach_interfaces/action/PalletTask "{mode: pickup}" --feedback

# ---------------- Goal ----------------
# "pickup"         the whole sequence, ending with the forks loaded.
#                  The only mode (D95); an empty string also means "pickup".
#                  Any other value is refused.
string mode
---
# ---------------- Result ----------------
# INSERTED  the whole sequence completed: forks in, lifted, backed out
# NO_GO     the rules refused, or the face could not be identified, or there
#           was not enough room to approach and the reverse could not be
#           justified. `reason` says which.
# NO_PALLET nothing was confirmed within the timeout
# ABORTED   cancelled, an unhealthy stack, a lost pallet, a controller abort
string outcome
string reason                         # why, with the numbers in it
string mode                           # which mode this run was asked for (only "pickup")

# Which face was entered. "short" or "long"; empty if it never got that far.
# Not a label: it selects the pocket nominals, the fork geometry and the
# insertion stop (D21/D22).
string side

# What the run ACHIEVED, not that it finished. insertion_depth is how far the
# robot drove into the pallet; pallet_lift is how far the pallet came off the
# floor, which is the carriage travel minus the slack above the tines and so
# differs between the two faces (D44). Both zero unless the outcome is
# INSERTED.
float32 insertion_depth
float32 pallet_lift

geometry_msgs/PoseStamped pallet_pose # last accepted estimate
---
# ---------------- Feedback ----------------
# CONFIRMING, CLASSIFYING, BACKING_OFF, CLOSING, CHECKING, LOWERING,
# INSERTING, LIFTING, BACKING_OUT
string phase
string reason                         # what the phase is waiting for
float32 distance_to_standoff          # metres still to close; negative = past it
float32 lateral_offset                # metres from the pocket centre line
float32 confidence                    # the tracker's, 0 to 1
